<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>27th January</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Battle</B> <P>
<font size="3">

The dwarf looked around him, his head jerking to and fro, searching for some unfortunate
Piece of furniture yet intact. With a swift kick the last of his chairs died a sickening
death crashed against the corners of his chamber. Even dwarven carpentry had no mission
faced with his anger. <P>

"I WILL NOT BE DENIED MY PRIZE", he fumed.<P>

"I cannot explain it my lord", the young dwarf stood tall despite his fear.<P>

"Where did she go? How can she run, she is bound to her wretched lair"<P>

"She did not run my lord"<P>

The dwarves breathing slowed.<P>

"What?"<P>

"We found her slain. Her lifeblood spilled and slewn around her lair, her guardians smashed"<P>

"Who DARES steal my quarry from me?"<P>

"We know not, but the rangers will not rest till we know master"<P>

The dwarves expression tightened. Pausing for thought he whispered.<P>

"The matter must be resolved before the Mistress finds out, or the heads of the
defilers will not be the only ones to roll this season". <P>

The silence confirmed the dwarves words. Almost invisible traces of frost on
their breaths suggesting they were being watched with an icy gaze.<P>

"Our warriors are mighty but they are old. They have families and responsibilities. Our crusades require
planning, and long communications with our allies to coordinate our efforts and
share the rewards. We will not stand for continued disruption of our plans."<P>

"Perhaps a warning m'lord?"<P>

"They were warned"<P>

"Perhaps a final warning then?"<P>

"This is the forth such incident, lad. It is easy to steal eggs from 
the birds nest when she defends her nest with her song and not her claws."<P>

"Until the new moon, for two dozen days and two dozen nights, the heads of those
who seek to undermine us will fall like rain upon the lands of Norrath. Perhaps
the rhythm of sword on sword will serve somewhat to lull my anger."<P>

"And the rules of the field my lord? Shall they be permitted to retrieve the
bodies of their fallen?"<P>

His master thought for a moment.<P>

"Take these seals of Kalidim. Permit their priests to pray for their dead
and recover their fallen, on the understanding that they will not return
to the lands where they were defeated that night. If they would return
before the dawn, place one of these three seals upon the corpses of their
dead. When you have no more seals, then our patience will be at an end."<P>

"As you wish it."<P>



</tr>
















<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>14th January</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Prepping for GOD</B> <P>
<font size="3">

We pushed another few Quarm kills under our belt, and survived the Christmass/New Year lull
with relativly few casulties. Right now were focused on gearing up our troops for the 
new expansion, it'll be interesting to see how guilds do across all the EQ servers as
the playing field has leveled considerably since the last expansion.<P>

<img src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/monsterpics/The_Seventh_Hammer.JPG" align="right" width="300" > <BR>

As well as our usual flag/time runs we found time to stick in another Server first with
the slaying of the Seventh hammer. Loots wernt exaclty great, but it was fun to finish 
up the POP content.<P>

Weve had a peek around LDON raids after our first success, and plan to have a blast
at some of the Time level LDON raids while we await the new expansion. We'll keep you
posted.<P>

<B>RECUITMENT</B>
<BR>
We are currently recuiting: Druids, Clerics, Necros, Bards , BST and Shaman.<P>

Please see our recuitment board for more details. Feel free to talk to current
Wudan initiates to see how they find the guild.<P>

Lastly, we finally found the gremlins in our DPS stats, and plan to have more
accurate and regularly updated DPS stats on or web front. Should have some
stats up here by the end of the day. Enjoy!<P>

<BR>
<BR>


</tr>





















<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>24th November</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Onwards ho!</B> <P>
<font size="3">

With our third Quarm kill PoP has been firmly pushed on the 'farming' shelf.<P>

<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/monsterpics/Innoruuk.jpg" align="right" width="150"> 


As ever the guild is looking for new challenges to test our steel, so we had a peek around Norrath
for some challenges which havent been meet yet on RZ. First on the list was the God everyone loves
to hate... (HATE.. Get it?????) Innourk. <P>

Sure.. we kicked his skinny bootie all over the Plane of Time, but the 'new and improved' version
in the funky new plane of hate remained unchallenged. Dropped w/o too much drama with a few
semi ok loots.<P>

<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/rpics/insidious_twisted_cord.jpg" > 
<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/rpics/beacon_of_loathing.jpg" > 
<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/Rustedwickedfaceguard.jpg" > <P>




<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/nov/corpse.jpg" align="right" width="400" > <BR>

After that, it was time we moved onto something a little more meaty. LDON. Love em or hate em
these raids are a nice challenge, with some interesting new concepts. Its been far too long
for an expansion to be out without any of its major heros being downed, so Wudan stepped
up. We're glad to say that Warlord Ojin is no longer terrorizing the deserts of Ro :).<P>



Loots wernt half bad actually, nice surprise was.. there were six of em.<P>

<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/nov/fourloots.jpg" > 
<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/nov/twoloots.jpg" > <P>


Heres a lil top tip for people raiding plane of time. Invis all your raiders
to confuse teh mobs:<BR>

<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/nov/spooky.jpg" > 


Still getting some fallout from the RZ Sleeper kill. This was a cool lil gesture
at the PoK bank:<BR>

<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/nov/seventh.jpg" > 

<P>

As you can prolly tell from our recuitment board, recuitment is currently slowing way down
as we have a nice steady compliment of raiders. Recuitment is still open on some classes
and we will open other classes as the need arises.<P>

Right now, Wudan are gonna concentrate on pushing forwards with new LDON content,and gearing
up to meet the new expansion head on.<P>



<BR>
<BR>


</tr>








<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>17th November</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>17th of November - An Historic date</B> <P>
<font size="3">


With the threat of common pk's buying Sleepers keys in the Bazar and taking it on themselves
to wake the Sleeper in ST, the three main powers on the server decided it was
time to do the needfull. With easy, fully geared server transfers, it was obvious it was only
a matter of time before the encounter was 'spoiled', and so.. Wudan, Ascending Dawn and Magus
set about killing the unkillable. <P>

Our plan on or first attempt on the Saturday was to wake the Sleeper and "See if we can dent him". 
Within the first few minutes
corpses rained, and we found out he quads for 7000 and procs 20k. As the fight progessed
we worked out a way to dent him. Last nights attempt was a lot tidier and we ended up fighting
the zone lag more than the Dragon.<P>


<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/sleeper/sleeper1.jpg" align="center" width="600" > <P>

The armies of Rallos Zek await the Sleeper.<P>

<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/sleeper/sleeper2.jpg" align="center" width="600" > <P>

There is much slaying to be done....<P>

<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/sleeper/sleeper3.jpg" align="center" width="600" > <P>

The corpse.<P>

<img  src="http://remus.cometway.com:8900/images/sleeper/sleeperdead.jpg" align="left"  > <P>

Grats Trylun you manaburn saving manwhore.<P>
<BR>
<BR>


This night more than any other demonstrates the unique culture on Rallos Zek. It's a server with daily
conflicts and nightly disputes, but its a server that allows us to set our own laws and enforce our
own rules. Its also a server that allows us to shape our own history. <P>

Big thanks to AD and MiM for one of the most memorable nights in EQ.<P>



</tr>














<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>15th November</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Strange things afoot at the circle-K!</B> <P>
<font size="3">



The party ducked awkwardly below the silvery arches of the Dwarven Capital.
The look on the tall Barbarian's face told what he thought of the dwarves
love of unnecessary architecture.<P>

He held his tongue. The atmosphere in the cold chamber was not comfortable. The
sooner they could complete their business the sooner they could be on their way.<P>

Taking the seats allocated to them near the head of the time worn table, they surveyed
the room of familiar faces.<P>

Across from them a small woodelf girl sat, drawing frequent glances from the
servants hurrying to take the cloaks of the new arrives. She entertained their
lingering gazes much to the irritation of her halfelven council by her side. Making
no secret of his unease he shoved his cloak a little too forcefully into the 
chest of a servant who had let his gaze linger a little too long. The young elf
afforded the servant an brief, apologetic smile.<P>

Further along the table, sat a Coercer sat shifting in her seat. The barbarian smiled.<P>

<i>As impatient as ever</i>, he thought to himself. <P>

Letting his mind wander, trying to deduce who whey were still waiting for, his attention 
turned to the skylight, watching the storm above intensify. As the first real peal of thunder
rippled down the halls, the barbarian noticed the first of the Coercers council, sitting 
calmly on a window ledge. <P>

With the next call of thunder the old druid removed the long pipe from his mouth 
and raised and eyebrow at his mistress. She shook her head quickly. The atmospherics seemed 
strangely fitting, and besides, the music of the storm filled the gap while they waited 
for the more tardy of their number.<P>

"So if I might ask" - The halfelf spoke irritably.<P>

"Who is it that keeps us waiting?"<P>

As if on que, a loud crash thundered from the stairs outside the door, accompanied
by an almighty stream of fluent swearing. The Coercer rolled her eyes, averting
her gaze from those around from her.<P>

"I'M ALL RIGHT! JUST GET OUT OF MY WAY".<P>

"Do you REALLY need all those?". The Coercer looked distainfully at the clatter of
weapons in the dwarves arms as he pushed his way past the servants scuttling out of his way.<P>

"They are SIT-U-ATION-AL" grumped the Dwarf.<P>

The coercer mimicked the dwarves words silently behind his back as he dropped
into his seat.<P>

"I believe that is all of us?", prompted the Barbarian.<P>

Taking her que from the words, the slight woodelf rose quietly to her
feet. The chair slid back as if of its own accord. The flirtatious smile gone, her
stony expression sent the servants away, melting into the archways like shadows
before a cold dawn.<P>

Leaning on the table with her knuckles the ancient timbers creaked ominously, as
if surprised by the force set upon them by such a slight figure. Her audience
seemed unmoved by the woodelf's change in demeanour. They knew her too well to
underestimate how seriously she took such matters.<P>

She spoke.<P>

"As it was written..."<P>

"CCCCCRRRAASHSSSSSH..BANG"<P>

The Coercer winced.<P>

"Sorriieeee" piped the dwarf. He glanced up bashfully. The Halfelf
smiled sarcastically in return.<P>

The Woodelf waited for the fallen swords to settle quietly on the floor.<P>

"As it was written", she continued.<P>

"The outsiders have found a way to access what was once denied to them"<P>

No questions were forthcoming. No explanations necessary.<P>

"We know what we must do. The events have been foreseen and our roles in this
are unavoidable. This night is the last you have to raise your voices against
the prophecy"<P>

None came forth.<P>

She lifted her hands from the table and stood back from the table.<P>

"COME!"<P>

The door creaked open and a hovelling misshapen figure slid into the room. The rooms
inhabitants averted their gaze unable to face looking directly at the twisted shape. All save
the dwarf who was unable to look away, his face twisted in pity and disgust.<P>

"Don't beats me mistress.... not today....". The words dropped on the floor like
drool from a mezmerized kobold's maw.<P>

"No beatings today my disgusting friend. Today I have a job for you"<P>

The figure stopped shaking. It's skin cracked as it's ears perked.

"No beatings?"<P>

"We have need of your kind. Summon the Darkones and prepare your place. You will
have guests this evening."<P>

The figure didn't need any more excuses to leave. It bolted for the door, its tiny
hands covering its head in anticipation of the blows from its mistress or her council. 
None came.<P>

"The wheel is turning. Make the neccessary preperations."<P>

The old druid on the window crossed his legs and pulled them close. He refilled his
pipe firmly, without watching his fingers, his gaze fixed on the stars above. Squinting
against Luclins glare he picked out his favourite constalations from the heavens as he
relit his pipe.<P>

He sighed.<P>

"I bet I get summoned...." <P>





</tr>















<tr>
	<td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#C0C0C0"><font color="#666666"><b>10th November</B></font>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	 <td width="536" height="26" bgcolor="#808080">
        <BR>


<B>Quarm dead - Steady on!</B> <P>
<font size="3">

<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/monsterpics/Quarm.JPG" align="center" width="500" > <P>

Hey! Just cause Wudan has won the game doesnt mean you  have to go and loose you head! <P>
See what I did there?<P>

Our second encounter with Inny did the needful, and we got our date with Quarm. Scrolling back through
our news archives, I see we've come a long way since we spent our nights pouring over our diagrams
of Trakanons lair, formulating plans to try and kill him for VP keys. <P>

I've said it before and I'll say it again. I expect _every_ member of wudan to perform well on our raids
but since I have the platform here a mention to a few people that have made the battles in poTime a 
little easier for one reason or another: Bashm, Quendara, Cenobita, Cland, Qument. <P>

Few highlights:<P>

Wilus: <BR>
<img  src="http://members.shaw.ca/kaganos/items/0056.gif" > <P>

Miladil: <BR>
<img  src="http://members.shaw.ca/kaganos/items/0065.gif" > <P>

Vishunu: <BR>
<img  src="http://members.shaw.ca/kaganos/items/0097.gif" > <P>

Ornette: <BR>
<img  src="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/kerashas_sylvan_tunic.jpg" > <P>

Elira: <BR>
<img  src="http://members.shaw.ca/kaganos/items/0124.gif" > <P>

Antha: <BR>
<img  src="http://members.shaw.ca/kaganos/items/0117.gif" > <P>

Rot (Yes I suck. Sue me): <BR>
<img  src="http://members.shaw.ca/kaganos/items/0119.gif" > (I think)<P>




As we have a comfortable raid contingent of around 70 for time raids recuitment is slowing way down. We've
stopped recuitment on some classes and increased AA requirments for all classes. Check this link for more
details:<BR>

<A href="http://www.waster.net/wudan/forum/index.php?act=ST&f=6&t=6101&s=13e8d25e6fd013afddf55eb00fb553b5">Requirments<A>
<P>

That brings the total to two, for RZ guilds that have cleared PoTime. Saying as there are less than 50 guilds
across all servers that have cleared time, and possibly no other Zek server clearings, I'm proud to see Rallos
Zek stake its claim high amongst the other servers.<P>




</tr>




















